{
  "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
  "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is that this -- there is a distinction between the, quote, \"appellate jurisdiction\" under 2104 and the original writ of certiorari which would lie in this Court in some instances."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You're saying the application is the application -- the petition for certiorari is the application?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I take it you're talking about language, if I followed it, in 2244(d)(2)."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Any -- any statistics on how many petitions for cert from state post-conviction collateral review are granted? In other words, if we are talking about an additional six months in every case, how many of those are actually granted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I suppose you'd have to file a protective petition with the district court saying we won but we might still lose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Kise, can I ask you what your view in this matter would be if the Court grants certiorari, would the application be pending during the period that the case is under advisement in this Court?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Is it, is it clear that he can go to district -- I mean, I'm not familiar with how these things work. Is it possible that when there is an appeal or certiorari pending here there can be proceeding in district court a habeas action on the same, on the same matter that we are considering on certiorari?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kise",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yes, Your Honor, I believe there can. I believe, there is, in fact --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Wouldn't a district judge who knows that there's a cert petition pending just say: Well, I'll wait; this petition will be held pending the Supreme Court's disposition of cert."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kise",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would respectfully say to Your Honor that it's not an automatic stay. I mean, perhaps there would be a stay at some point. But there are things that can be accomplished in Federal court before the undertaking of the review. There is the Rule 4 screening process in habeas. There is the initial review by the district court to see if the filing itself meets the procedural requirements. There is the asking for an answer by the state. There is discovery that can take place."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But isn't it true the real problem with the capital cases? The state's interest in getting things moving is the strongest in the capital cases, I think."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Kise",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Honor. What I would say is the time -- certain time is consumed just determining whether or not under the Rule 4 screening process, whether or not the petition meets the formal requirements, whether they've articulated the claim in the correct way and whether it's worthy of the state response, if there's discovery that needs to be had."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Bonner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, respectfully, Your Honor -- and I know that that is the petitioner's argument and I see that you have given me that question, but I don't know that it is that much of a choice. I mean, I think that they can file, they can file both in those circumstances and, and depending on the particular circumstances -- and this is back to the equitable tolling principles -- for statutory tolling purposes, I think the answer is they must file both or they forfeit the right to one or the other."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I guess you could also say that except in capital cases the defendant will not have an incentive to delay. He wants to get out, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Bonner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "case I was looking at statistics as to the average length of time that a case was pending before, between conviction and the filing of the 2254, and Mr. Lawrence's petition was filed within days of what the average was before the AEDPA. That comes up in a statistical analysis I believe by the Department of Justice cited to by the state."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Bonner",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "60f83a2440e187c2870c14c86c51dd16ed68315d6a03341294cd03d9f4c1b2ce",
      "evidence_id": "ev-60f83a2440e1-0002-0009",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Also, whether it's 90 days or six months as Your Honor has said, it's always in the control of this Court. Once the 90 -- this is not a frolic of unnumbered years. When someone files a petition he either files it by the time 90 days is over or he is out of court, or he files it and this Court is quickly reviewing it after some input from the other side."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-8820",
